<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15947" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕpĭgramma</span></b> ,
			ătis, n. (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>dat. plur.</i> epigrammatis, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				1, 16, 15</span></i>.—<i>Gen. plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">epigrammatōn,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 1 praef.</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 2</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-matum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 85</span></i>
			), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίγραμμα</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An inscription;</i> on the base of a statue, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2,
				4, 57</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">on an offering,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep.
					Paus. 1, 3</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">on tombstones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 115 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">as a brand,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 103, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An epigram</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				1, 34, 84</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Arch. 10, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 1,
				5, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 73</span></i> et saep.; so the
			Epigrammata of the poet Martial.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
